      "testable_prediction": "An adaptive $q$ variant will yield an improved F1-score across multi-density contaminated datasets compared to any fixed global $q \\in \\{2,3,4,5,6\\}$.",
      "caveats": "May increase computational overhead during iteration due to local density estimation."
    },
    {
      "hypothesis": "Assuming that the true data-generating process of regular observations follows a multivariate Gaussian distribution, expressing the null distribution of pseudo-isolations $Y$ in closed-form via chi-square mixture approximations will yield tighter false-alarm bounds and elevate individual anomaly detection from conservative bounding to exact hypothesis testing.",
